{{also|Areola|aréola}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Weibliche brust en.jpg|right|thumb|A woman's breasts, with the areola indicated.]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|āreola||small vacant space, garden}}, diminutive of {{m|la|ārea}}. {{doublet|en|areole}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/əˈɹi.ə.lə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/əˈɹi.ə.lə/|/ˌɛ.ɹiˈoʊ.lə/|/ˌæ.ɹiˈoʊ.lə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|areolae|areolæ}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The colored [[circle]] around a [[nipple]], more exactly known as [[areola mammae]].
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Any small circular area that is different from its immediate environment, such as the colored ring around the [[pupil]] of the [[eye]] ([[iris]]) or an inflamed region surrounding a [[pimple]].
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Any of the small spaces throughout [[w:loose connective tissue|areolar connective tissue]].
#* '''1847''', ''The Medico-Chirurgical Review'', volume 51, page 329:
#*: The tubes or elongated spaces of which we have spoken, are not distended with any fluid, but are merely moistened in the same way as the '''areolas''' of ordinary areolar tissue.

====Usage notes====
* Not to be confused with {{m|en|aureola}}.

